```

Definitions hold static arrays; applied packages and operations are entities.
`applyEffectInstance()`, `removeEffectInstance()`, and
`snapshotEffectInstances()` are the canonical lifecycle facade. An effect
outlives a consumed source item. Attribution retains the source item ID, source
identity, and applying actor; the item is not its lifetime owner.

| Stacking policy | Reapplication |
| --- | --- |
| `refresh` (default) | Keep one instance, maximum remaining duration/potency, preserve periodic cadence |
| `extend` | Add remaining duration, preserve cadence |
| `replace` | Remove the prior package and apply a new lifetime |
| `stack` | Increase stacks up to `maxStacks`, refresh duration and scale operations |
| `independent` | Create another independent package |

Matching is by `definition` (default), applying `actor`, or source `item`.
Finite effects cannot shorten permanent effects through refresh/extension.
`turnsLeft: Infinity` represents permanence. Expiry, explicit removal, curing,
replacement, and actor death remove the package and its operation children.
Immunities to the definition or one of its semantic statuses prevent application.

An application does not perform periodic operations immediately. Each subsequent
positive simulation turn advances its operations once. Onset pauses both the
lifetime countdown and operation cadence. The final turn performs due operations
before expiry. Duplicate processing at the same simulation time and zero-delta
UI ticks do not advance a package. The existing effects phase owns execution;
there are no new scheduler phases or system-to-system calls.

## Activation and presentation

Inventory use and quick slots carry the selected ability ID. Main-layer targeting
collects a target before dispatching `UseIntent`; it performs no ability mutation.
The use pipeline revalidates ownership, living targets, faction, range, line of
sight, equipment requirements, charges, and cooldowns. Headless/AI callers can
submit the same intent. Enemy and untargeted actions have UI support; ally targets
can currently be supplied by rules callers.

Ability effects, scripted local state, charge costs, and cooldowns are queued in
the existing interaction transaction. Cancellation discards the queued changes.
A valid attempt against an immune target still spends the activation cost.
Charges belong to the item entity. Items with `Charges` or `ScriptState` do not
merge their simulation state into another item stack.

`EffectChanged` records application, refresh, and removal; `ItemAbilityActivated`
records successful activation. These are concrete events, not string aliases.
Existing authored activation presentations remain available through `ctx.present()`.

HUD and character details share `buildEffectRows()`. Independent packages retain
separate instance IDs, and VIS badges use those IDs. Permanent badges display
infinity. Projection restores persistent badges without emitting activation events.

## Persistence and migration

Game save/export uses `serializeSavegameWorld()` so absolute item cooldowns retain
the game turn. The registry includes `ItemCooldown`, `ScriptState`, and the new
effect components. Load restores permanent durations from the explicit lifecycle
flag after JSON serialization turns `Infinity` into `null`.

Town Stew is the first migrated definition. Legacy `town_stew` array records are
materialized through the canonical facade and removed before legacy resolution,
so they cannot tick twice. Other legacy effect families retain their existing
resolver while they are migrated incrementally.

## Subsequent milestones

The first slice provides control statuses, periodic operations, charges, named
activation, persistence, and shared visual identity. Remaining work from the
architecture plan includes authored stat/proc children with lifecycle-aware
traversal, percentage movement/attack timing, scoped immunity definitions,
persistent world VFX profiles, and incremental migration of other legacy families.
New definitions should extend these shared surfaces as those capabilities land.
import { EFFECT_DEFS } from "./effectDefs.js";

const definitions = new Map();
const OPERATIONS = new Set(["damage", "heal", "stamina_restore", "mana_restore", "mana_drain", "stamina_drain"]);

// Static authoring registry. Runtime state is always stored on attached entities.
export function registerEffectDefinition(id, def) {
  if (!/^[a-z][a-z0-9_]*$/.test(id) || definitions.has(id)) throw new Error(`Invalid or duplicate effect definition: ${id}`);
  if (!def || typeof def !== "object") throw new Error(`Missing effect definition: ${id}`);
  const stacking = def.stacking || "refresh";
  if (!["refresh", "extend", "replace", "stack", "independent"].includes(stacking)) throw new Error(`Invalid effect stacking: ${stacking}`);
  const maxStacks = def.maxStacks ?? 1;
  if (!Number.isInteger(maxStacks) || maxStacks < 1) throw new Error("Effect maxStacks must be a positive integer");
  const match = def.match || "definition";
  if (!["definition", "actor", "item"].includes(match)) throw new Error(`Invalid effect match: ${match}`);
  if (def.periodic != null && !Array.isArray(def.periodic)) throw new Error("Effect periodic operations must be an array");
  if (def.statuses != null && (!Array.isArray(def.statuses) || def.statuses.some((key) => typeof key !== "string" || !key))) throw new Error("Effect statuses must be non-empty strings");
  const periodic = (def.periodic || []).map((op) => {
    if (!OPERATIONS.has(op.operation)) throw new Error(`Unknown periodic operation: ${op.operation}`);
    if (!Number.isFinite(op.amount) || op.amount < 0) throw new Error("Effect amount must be non-negative");
    const interval = op.interval ?? 1;
    if (!Number.isInteger(interval) || interval < 1) throw new Error("Effect interval must be a positive integer");
    return Object.freeze({ ...op, interval });
  });
  const out = Object.freeze({ ...def, id, stacking, maxStacks, match, statuses: Object.freeze([...(def.statuses || [])]), periodic: Object.freeze(periodic) });
  definitions.set(id, out);
  return out;
}

export function getEffectDefinition(id) {
  return definitions.get(String(id || "").toLowerCase()) || null;
}

const stew = EFFECT_DEFS.find((def) => def.id === "town_stew");
registerEffectDefinition("town_stew", {
  name: "Town Stew",
  description: stew.description,
  visualIdentity: "food_stew",
  statuses: stew.statuses,
  periodic: stew.operations.map((operation) => ({ operation, amount: 1 })),
});
import { assert, assertEquals } from "jsr:@std/assert";
import { World } from "../src/lib/ecs-js/index.js";
import { defineEffect, defineItem } from "../src/content/define.js";
import { getContentItem } from "../src/content/registry.js";
import { createContentAbilityController } from "../src/main/targeting/itemAbilityController.js";
import { registerCatalogItem } from "../src/rules/data/itemCatalog.js";
import { Charges, Faction, Inventory, NamedIdentity, Position, Vitality } from "../src/rules/components/index.js";
import { ScriptState } from "../src/rules/components/ScriptState.js";
import { UseIntent } from "../src/rules/components/Intents/UseIntent.js";
import { ItemAbilityActivated } from "../src/events/ItemAbilityActivated.js";
import { useItemSystem } from "../src/rules/systems/useItemSystem.js";
import { addToInventory, removeFromInventory } from "../src/rules/utils/inventoryFacade.js";
import { getItemCooldownRemaining } from "../src/rules/utils/itemCooldowns.js";
import { statusStrength } from "../src/rules/utils/statusFacade.js";
import { snapshotEffectInstances } from "../src/rules/utils/effectInstances.js";
import { createItemById } from "../src/rules/utils/itemFactory.js";
import { clearAll, loadChunk, setTile } from "../src/rules/environment/dungeon/tileMap.js";
import { Player } from "../src/rules/components/Player.js";
import { serializeSavegameWorld } from "../src/main/wiring/savegameSerializationRegistry.js";
import { restoreSnapshotFromSavegame } from "../src/main/wiring/savegameLoad.js";
import { CHUNK_SIZE, TILE_FLOOR, TILE_WALL } from "../src/rules/environment/dungeon/constants.js";
import { buildWorldView } from "../src/bridge/schema/worldView.js";

defineEffect("test_charm_stun", { name: "Tidal Stun", statuses: ["stunned"], periodic: [] });
defineItem("test_charged_charm", {
  name: "Test Charm", type: "tool", chargePool: { current: 2, max: 2 }, state: { invoked: false },
  abilities: {
    stun: { targeting: "enemy", range: 4, cooldown: 3, chargeCost: 1, effects: [{ key: "test_charm_stun", turnsLeft: 3 }] },
    cancel: { cooldown: 3, chargeCost: 1, onActivate(ctx) { ctx.setState({ invoked: true }); ctx.setCooldown(20); ctx.cancel({ code: "TEST_CANCEL", message: "Cancelled" }); } },
    stateful: { onActivate(ctx) { ctx.setState({ invoked: true }); ctx.setState({ count: 1 }); ctx.setState({ count: ctx.state().count + 1 }); } },
  },
});
registerCatalogItem("test_charged_charm", getContentItem("test_charged_charm"));

function setup() {
  clearAll();
  loadChunk(-1, -1, new Uint8Array(CHUNK_SIZE * CHUNK_SIZE).fill(TILE_FLOOR));
  const world = new World({ seed: 614 });
  const actor = world.create();
  world.add(actor, Player, {});
  world.add(actor, Inventory, { capacity: 20 });
  world.add(actor, Vitality, { hp: 10, maxHp: 10 });
  world.add(actor, Faction, { key: "player" });
  world.add(actor, Position, { x: -8, y: -8 });
  const item = createItemById(world, "test_charged_charm");
  addToInventory(world, actor, item);
  const target = world.create();
  world.add(target, NamedIdentity, { identity: "goblin", name: "Goblin" });
  world.add(target, Vitality, { hp: 10, maxHp: 10 });
  world.add(target, Faction, { key: "enemy" });
  world.add(target, Position, { x: -6, y: -8 });
  world.setScheduler(useItemSystem);
  const activate = (abilityId = "stun") => {
    let result;
    const off = world.on("interaction:result", (event) => { result = event; });
    world.add(actor, UseIntent, { itemId: item, targetId: target, abilityId });
    useItemSystem(world);
    off();
    return result;
  };
  return { world, actor, item, target, activate };
}

Deno.test("named item activation applies targeted topology effects and commits charge/cooldown once", () => {
  const { world, actor, item, target, activate } = setup();
  const receipts = [];
  world.on(ItemAbilityActivated, (event) => receipts.push(event));
  assert(activate().ok);
  assertEquals(statusStrength(world, target, "stunned"), 1);
  assert(buildWorldView(world).entities.find((entry) => entry.id === target)?.tags.includes("stunned"));
  assertEquals(snapshotEffectInstances(world, target)[0].sourceId, item);
  assertEquals(world.get(item, Charges).current, 1);
  assertEquals(getItemCooldownRemaining(world, item), 3);
  assertEquals(receipts.map((event) => [event.actor, event.itemId, event.targetId, event.abilityId]), [[actor, item, target, "stun"]]);
  assertEquals(activate().reason, "ABILITY_COOLDOWN");
  assertEquals(world.get(item, Charges).current, 1);
  assertEquals(receipts.length, 1);
});

Deno.test("invalid target, range, sight, charges, and ownership reject before costs", () => {
  for (const condition of ["dead", "friendly", "range", "wall", "charges", "ownership"]) {
    const { world, item, target, actor, activate } = setup();
    if (condition === "dead") world.get(target, Vitality).hp = 0;
    if (condition === "friendly") world.get(target, Faction).key = "player";
    if (condition === "range") world.get(target, Position).x = -1;
    if (condition === "wall") setTile(-7, -8, TILE_WALL);
    if (condition === "charges") world.get(item, Charges).current = 0;
    if (condition === "ownership") removeFromInventory(world, actor, item);
    assert(!activate().ok, condition);
    assertEquals(world.get(item, Charges).current, condition === "charges" ? 0 : 2, condition);
    assertEquals(getItemCooldownRemaining(world, item), 0, condition);
    assertEquals(snapshotEffectInstances(world, target).length, 0, condition);
  }
});

Deno.test("cancelled scripted activation discards state, effects, charges, and cooldown", () => {
  const { world, item, activate } = setup();
  assertEquals(activate("cancel").reason, "TEST_CANCEL");
  assertEquals(world.get(item, ScriptState).data.invoked, false);
  assertEquals(world.get(item, Charges).current, 2);
  assertEquals(getItemCooldownRemaining(world, item), 0);
});

Deno.test("target selection spends nothing until confirmation and rules revalidate moved targets", () => {
  const { world, actor, item, target } = setup();
  let prompt;
  const request = createContentAbilityController({
    world,
    targeting: { openEnemyTargeting: (spec) => { prompt = spec; } },
    playerEntity: () => ({ id: actor, pos: world.get(actor, Position) }),
    scanVisibleEnemies: () => [{ id: target }],
  });
  assert(request(item, "stun"));
  assert(prompt);
  assertEquals(world.step, 0);
  assertEquals(world.get(item, Charges).current, 2);
  world.get(target, Position).x = -1;
  prompt.onConfirm(target);
  assertEquals(world.get(item, Charges).current, 2);
  assertEquals(getItemCooldownRemaining(world, item), 0);
  assertEquals(snapshotEffectInstances(world, target), []);
});

Deno.test("scripted activation reads its own queued state patches and commits them together", () => {
  const { world, item, activate } = setup();
  assert(activate("stateful").ok);
  assertEquals(world.get(item, ScriptState).data, { invoked: true, count: 2 });
});

Deno.test("charged ability cooldown and charges resume on the saved game turn", () => {
  const { world, actor, item, activate } = setup();
  world.step = 100;
  assert(activate().ok);
  const snapshot = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify({ world: serializeSavegameWorld(world) }));
  const restored = new World({ seed: 614 });
  restoreSnapshotFromSavegame(restored, snapshot);
  assertEquals(restored.step, 100);
  assertEquals(restored.get(item, Charges).current, 1);
  assertEquals(getItemCooldownRemaining(restored, item), 3);
  assertEquals(restored.get(item, ScriptState).data, { invoked: false });
});

Deno.test("two copies retain independent charge pools instead of merging into an item stack", () => {
  const { world, actor, item, activate } = setup();
  assert(activate().ok);
  const second = createItemById(world, "test_charged_charm");
  assert(addToInventory(world, actor, second));
  assert(world.isAlive(second));
  assertEquals(world.get(item, Charges).current, 1);
  assertEquals(world.get(second, Charges).current, 2);
});
